# Retire leaked ychrome daemons on this host, whatever HOME namespace they
# were spawned under. `daemon reap` is safe by construction
# (docs/host-daemon.md §6.2): it identifies daemons from kernel facts
# (daemon.lock FDs in /proc), sends retire_if_idle to each daemon's OWN
# socket, and a daemon refuses unless it is genuinely idle (no attached
# session, no engine page). Only unreachable zombies — lock held, nothing
# answering — are retired outright.

[Unit]
Description=ychrome: retire leaked or stale daemons across all HOME roots

[Service]
Type=oneshot
ExecStart=%h/.local/bin/ychrome daemon reap
# A non-zero exit means the census itself failed (never that a daemon was
# busy — reap reports and exits 0). Keep the failure visible in the journal.
